@startuml ref-cli-surface
title Claude Code CLI surfaces used by mcp-emacs
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #888888
  BackgroundColor #F7F7F7
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #4472A8
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  FontColor #4472A8
}

rectangle "claude (CLI)" as CLI #EAF0F8

package "1. TUI runner (mcp-emacs-run)" {
  rectangle "eat terminal buffer\n*claude:<project>:<n>*" as Eat
}
package "2. Headless one-shot (mcp-emacs-run)" {
  rectangle "make-process\n-p PROMPT --output-format text" as Headless
}
package "3. Stream runner (claude-client)" {
  rectangle "make-process\n--print --output-format stream-json\n--input-format stream-json" as Stream
}

package "Editor-tool channels" {
  rectangle "MCP over HTTP\nlocalhost:8765/mcp\n(mcp-emacs-server)" as MCP
  rectangle "IDE over WebSocket\n127.0.0.1:<random>\n(mcp-emacs-ide)" as IDE
}

Eat --> CLI : ANSI TUI, keystrokes in
Headless --> CLI : stdout text
Stream --> CLI : NDJSON both ways

CLI --> MCP : tools/list, tools/call\n(--mcp-config / user config)
CLI --> IDE : openDiff, getDiagnostics,\ncloseAllDiffTabs, close_tab\n(CLAUDE_CODE_SSE_PORT env)

note bottom of IDE
  Only reached when the CLI is launched with
  CLAUDE_CODE_SSE_PORT + ENABLE_IDE_INTEGRATION.
  Gates the CLI's *native* Edit/Write.
end note

note bottom of MCP
  Always available to any MCP client.
  Gates edits via apply_diff when the CLI's
  own Edit/Write are disallowed.
end note
@enduml
